From: NLauncher <opensource@nlauncher.net>
Subject: [PATCH] android: never use large pages / SysV shm

Termux links HotSpot against libandroid-shmem to emulate SysV shared
memory, which is only used for -XX:+UseSHM large pages. We do not ship
that library: shmget()/shmat() exist in bionic since API 26, so libjvm
links fine with API 29, and on Android we force all large page modes off
(SELinux denies SysV shm to apps, hugetlbfs is not available).
---

diff --git a/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp b/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp
--- a/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp
@@ -3979,6 +3979,17 @@
     return;
   }
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+  // Android apps cannot use SysV shared memory (blocked by SELinux) and
+  // hugetlbfs is not exposed to them. Never use large pages.
+  if (!FLAG_IS_DEFAULT(UseLargePages) || !FLAG_IS_DEFAULT(UseTransparentHugePages) ||
+      !FLAG_IS_DEFAULT(UseHugeTLBFS) || !FLAG_IS_DEFAULT(UseSHM)) {
+    log_warning(pagesize)("Large pages are not supported on Android; ignoring large page flags.");
+  }
+  UseLargePages = UseTransparentHugePages = UseHugeTLBFS = UseSHM = false;
+  return;
+#endif
+
   if (!FLAG_IS_DEFAULT(UseLargePages) && !UseLargePages) {
     // The user explicitly turned off large pages.
     // Ignore the rest of the large pages flags.
-- 
nlauncher-jre-android
